*Solution Steps Walkthrough:*
1. Compute partial derivatives of $x$ and $y$ with respect to $s$ and $t$.
2. Express $(partial f)/(partial s)$ and $(partial f)/(partial t)$ in terms of $(partial f)/(partial x)$ and $(partial f)/(partial y)$ using the chain rule.
3. Substitute these expressions into the original PDE to simplify it.
4. Convert the simplified PDE into the new coordinates $x$ and $y$ to get $(partial f)/(partial x) = x$.
5. Integrate with respect to $x$, introducing an arbitrary function $g(y)$.
6. Back-substitute $x$ and $y$ to get the final solution.
